    "created_at": "2025-12-21T12:10:59Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-21T12:10:59Z",
    "body": "This does seem like a genuine area of underspecification.\n\nAs I understand it, tabindex=\"-1\" removes an element from sequential focus navigation while still allowing programmatic focus. However, radio inputs already have special focus behavior where only one radio per group participates in tab navigation and arrow-key navigation is used within the group.\n\nWhat’s unclear to me from the spec is how these two models are intended to interact. In particular, it’s not obvious whether a radio with tabindex=\"-1\":\n\nshould be excluded entirely from the group’s focus handling, or\nshould only be skipped during sequential focus navigation while still participating in group navigation semantics.\n\nExplicitly clarifying this interaction in the spec (for example, with a short note or example for radio groups) could help align expectations between authors and implementations.",
